  "release_notes_md": "v0.1.6 closes two errors that v0.1.5 lab verification surfaced post-wizard.\n\n**api `0c06fe7` develop**:\n- **#22** alerts.py:ensure_tables() ran CREATE TABLE / CREATE INDEX / ALTER TABLE on every /alerts/* request with zero locking. When the portal swapped to the dashboard right after wizard finalize, concurrent /alerts/?... and /alerts/hourly?... requests raced on pg_class_relname_nsp_index \u2192 transient 500s. Same class of race v0.1.3 closed for main schema-init via pg_advisory_xact_lock. Hoisted alerts DDL into _run_migrations; alerts.py:ensure_tables stays as idempotent defense-in-depth.\n- **#23** cdp_v2_reprobe selected c.device_model \u2014 column was never defined in any schema. The error was masked pre-v0.1.5 by the camera_credentials UndefinedTableError on the same JOIN; v0.1.5 closed the table error, exposing this dead column reference. Dropped from query.\n\nOther repos: no-op tag bumps. Recommended for every v0.1.5 install.",
